-# Linux export for the Steam Deck and desktop Linux (docs/tools/steam-deck.md; the cloud report docs/tools/cloud-reports/2026-10-28-ci-linux.md).
-# Exports the project's "Linux" preset (release, Compatibility, x86_64, pck embedded) headless with the pinned Godot and template from setup-godot, sets the
-# executable bit, then plays the game's own bench headless twice, from the project and from the exported binary, and fails unless both print the same gameplay
-# hash at the same tick (the binary boots, loads its pck and plays the same match). Uploads the binary as a workflow artifact. By hand only. Nothing binary is committed.
-name: Linux export
-
-on:
-  workflow_dispatch:
-    inputs:
-      frames:
-        description: 'Frames (= ticks at --fixed-fps 60) the bench plays before it prints the gameplay hash'
-        required: false
-        default: '2400'
-
-permissions:
-  contents: read
-
-jobs:
-  linux:
-    name: Linux export (x86_64), headless boot and hash check
-    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04
-    timeout-minutes: 30
-    env:
-      FRAMES: ${{ inputs.frames }}
-    steps:
-      - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7.0.1
